{"id":1,"part":1,"title":"The Second Question","level":"A2","focus":"请求重复、确认时间、提出替代安排","story":"My bag is outside the door. My phone is in my hand.\n\nApartment 4B.\n\nI check the number again. Then I knock.\n\nA woman opens the door. She has a blue cup in one hand.\n\n“Andy?”\n\n“Yes. Hi. I’m Andy.”\n\n“I’m Maya. Come in.”\n\nI pick up my bag and follow her.\n\nThe apartment smells of coffee. There are two chairs by the window and a small table between them. One chair has books on it.\n\n“Sorry about the books,” Maya says. “Your room’s this way.”\n\nThe room is small, but it has a desk. I put my bag beside the bed.\n\n“Is it okay?” she asks.\n\n“Yes. It’s nice.”\n\nThere are other things I want to ask. Where can I put my food? Does the washing machine work? Why is there a bucket in the kitchen?\n\nBut Maya’s phone rings.\n\nShe looks at the screen and turns off the sound.\n\n“Sorry. Work.”\n\n“No problem.”\n\nMy bag falls over in the hall. A shoe comes out. We both look at it.\n\n“Sorry.” I push the shoe back with my foot.\n\n“Leave it open,” she says. “I left my bag here for a week.”\n\n“How long have you been here?”\n\n“Three years.”\n\nI look at the books on the chair again. On top is a picture of two people on a bus. One is asleep on the other one's shoulder.\n\n“Did you draw that?”\n\n“Yes.” For the first time she puts her phone down. “It's for a page I'm making. Look here.”\n\nShe turns the picture round. The people have the same coat. I see it now. The coat goes over both of them.\n\n“I like the man on the right,” I say.\n\n“That's my mum.”\n\nI look again. She laughs. “She really has that hat.”\n\nThe phone lights up. Maya looks at the name. This time she picks it up.\n\n“Work again?”\n\n“Yes. They want a new picture on somebody else's page. Mine can wait.”\n\nShe closes the book on the two people and their one coat.\n\nWe go back to the kitchen.\n\n“Tea?” she asks.\n\n“Yes, please.”\n\n“Milk?”\n\n“No, thanks.”\n\nGood. I can do this.\n\nMaya puts a cup in front of me. Then she points to the bucket.\n\n“The kitchen tap’s broken. Someone’s coming tomorrow, between eight and twelve. Can you be here? I’ve got to go to the office.”\n\nI hear tomorrow. I hear eight.\n\n“Yes,” I say.\n\nMaya picks up her phone.\n\n“Great. Thank you.”\n\nI look at the bucket. A drop of water falls into it.\n\nThen another.\n\nI have a meeting tomorrow at ten. My office is forty minutes away.\n\nPerhaps the man will come at eight. Perhaps the work will take ten minutes.\n\nPerhaps I should ask.\n\nMaya starts to type.\n\n“Sorry,” I say.\n\nShe looks up.\n\n“Could you say that again? The time?”\n\n“Between eight and twelve.”\n\n“Eight and twelve,” I repeat. “So, maybe eleven?”\n\n“Yes. We don’t have an exact time.”\n\n“Oh. I’m sorry. I have to leave at nine.”\n\nMaya puts her phone down.\n\n“Right.”\n\nFor a moment, neither of us speaks.\n\n“I can stay until nine,” I say. “Is that okay?”\n\n“Not really. He might come later.”\n\nMy face feels hot. I look at my tea.\n\nThen I try another question.\n\n“Can he come in the afternoon?”\n\nMaya looks at her phone.\n\n“I don’t know. Let me ask.”\n\nShe types a message. I move my cup away from the edge of the table.\n\nA minute later, her phone makes a sound.\n\n“Two to four,” she says. “I can be home then.”\n\n“So I don’t need to stay?”\n\n“That’s right.”\n\n“Okay. Sorry about that.”\n\n“It’s okay.” She picks up her cup. “Just tell me when you’re not sure.”\n\nHer phone rings again.\n\n“I need to take this. Make yourself at home.”\n\n“Thanks.”\n\nShe walks towards her room.\n\nI look at the two chairs by the window. Then I look at the books.\n\n“Maya?”\n\n“Yes?”\n\n“Can I move these?”\n\n“Of course. Put them on the table.”\n\nI move the books and sit down.\n\nMy tea is still warm.","practice":{"phrases":[{"en":"Could you say that again?","zh":"没听清时请求重复"},{"en":"I have to leave at nine.","zh":"说明自己的时间限制"},{"en":"I can stay until nine.","zh":"说明可以待到什么时候"},{"en":"Can he come in the afternoon?","zh":"提出替代安排"},{"en":"Let me ask.","zh":"表示需要向别人确认"}],"grammar":"between eight and twelve 是一个时间范围；until nine 表示一直到九点。把八点至十二点、两点至四点各说一次，再用自己的日程造句。","pronunciation":"按意群说：I can STAY / until NINE。先清楚表达时间，再把整句连起来，不用追求快。","questions":[{"q":"What is broken?","a":"The kitchen tap is broken."},{"q":"Why can’t Andy stay all morning?","a":"He has to leave at nine for a meeting at ten."},{"q":"What is the new time?","a":"Between two and four in the afternoon."}],"roleplay":{"context":"你刚搬进公寓，对方想请你等维修人员。先听对方，再用自己的时间回答。","turns":[{"line":"Someone is coming tomorrow morning. Can you be here?","cue":"询问具体时间，不要立刻答应。"},{"line":"Between eight and twelve.","cue":"说明你九点必须离开。"},{"line":"Then we need a different time.","cue":"询问能否改到下午。"}]},"transfer":"改成预约送货：你下午两点到五点在家。先说明能在家的时间，再请求对方确认。","retell":"用四句说清楚：Andy 到哪里、答应什么、有什么困难、最后怎样解决。"},"sentences":[{"id":"1-1","paragraph":0,"text":"My bag is outside the door.","charStart":0,"charEnd":27,"start":2.35,"end":3.8075},{"id":"1-2","paragraph":0,"text":"My phone is in my hand.","charStart":28,"charEnd":51,"start":4.1,"end":5.32},{"id":"1-3","paragraph":1,"text":"Apartment 4B.","charStart":53,"charEnd":66,"start":5.6125,"end":6.72},{"id":"1-4","paragraph":2,"text":"I check the number again.","charStart":68,"charEnd":93,"start":7.025,"end":8.1075},{"id":"1-5","paragraph":2,"text":"Then I knock.","charStart":94,"charEnd":107,"start":8.4125,"end":9.082499999999998},{"id":"1-6","paragraph":3,"text":"A woman opens the door.","charStart":109,"charEnd":132,"start":9.375,"end":10.745},{"id":"1-7","paragraph":3,"text":"She has a blue cup in one hand.","charStart":133,"charEnd":164,"start":11.05,"end":12.77},{"id":"1-8","paragraph":4,"text":"“Andy?”","charStart":166,"charEnd":173,"start":13.1375,"end":13.419999999999998},{"id":"1-9","paragraph":5,"text":"“Yes.","charStart":175,"charEnd":180,"start":13.7625,"end":14.12},{"id":"1-10","paragraph":5,"text":"Hi.","charStart":181,"charEnd":184,"start":14.5,"end":14.8575},{"id":"1-11","paragraph":5,"text":"I’m Andy.”","cha